        "original_id": "4c291337-2f6c-5dae-b002-f9acdeb9edbf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Draiman, Kip Winger, Dan Donegan, Mike Wengren, Steve \"Fuzz\" Kmak, Rod Morgenstein, Fiona\n- Bands: Disturbed, Device, Winger\n- Roles: vocalist, songwriter, guitarist, drummer, bassist, rock musician, solo artist, singer/bassist\n- Works: Disturbed discography, Heart Like a Gun, \"Everything You Do (You're Sexing Me)\"\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Frederick Kip Winger was born on June 21, 1961, and he is an American rock musician, a member of the band Winger, and a solo artist.\n- David Michael Draiman was born on March 13, 1973, and he is an American songwriter and the vocalist for Disturbed and Device.\n- Disturbed formed in 1996 when Dan Donegan, Mike Wengren, and Steve \"Fuzz\" Kmak hired David Draiman as vocalist.\n- The album Heart Like a Gun features Kip Winger and Rod Morgenstein from Winger.\n- On Heart Like a Gun, Kip Winger duets with Fiona on \"Everything You Do (You're Sexing Me)\".",
